  "placementWhy": "Similarity fit on two cenotes seen on the Esri satellite: the Carwash pool (dark pond about 40 x 35 m by the Coba road) and Luke's Hope (a small dark round opening on the Zacil-Ha grounds); both database points are Google Maps, 15-25 m off these openings, none from Open Caves. Checks, all independent of the fit: the fitted scale (0.2353 m/px) matches the printed scale bar (300 ft = 388 px, 0.2357 m/px) within 0.2%; the fitted rotation is only 0.5 deg from the map's (magnetic 1990) north; the map's Coba road (double dashed line, bearing about 316 deg) lands parallel to and on the real road, and the pool's drawn distance to the road (about 50 m) matches the satellite. No other map placed nearby (Camilo's walls end 700 m south). Not checked on the ground: the Luke's Hope = Zacil-Ha identification rests on the database's English name for Zacil-Ha, and on the map and satellite giving the same distance (214 vs 212 m) and bearing to Carwash.",
